# `constitution regen` fails with a precise error when a rule's category
# isn't in the configured vocabulary (M1 DoD: malformed ADRs fail with
# precise file/field errors; spec §2.5's hard-error stance). In v0.2 the
# unknown category arrives via a rule's "### <category>" tag.

! exec constitution regen
stderr 'field "category": rule bogus/some-rule: not in the configured category vocabulary \[architecture\] \(got "bogus"\)'
! stdout .
! exists constitution/constitution.md

-- constitution.yml --
schemaVersion: 1
categories:
  - architecture

-- constitution/adr/ADR-0001-bad-category.md --
---
id: ADR-0001
title: A rule with an unknown category
date: 2026-07-01
status: accepted
---

